devswarm_prompt.child_plan_key	{"v":"child-turn-plan"}
devswarm_prompt.child_receive	{"v":"💡 anti-hall · devswarm-child-reception: to RECEIVE parent messages, run `{cli} inbox pull <DEVSWARM_BUILDER_ID>` (anti-hall devswarm CLI) — a SAFE, bounded drain that folds the native parent->child queue into your durable inbox (non-destructive count gate, one bounded read, never `monitor`). Then read them via `{cli} inbox read-primary <DEVSWARM_BUILDER_ID>` (read-only; after handling, run the `ackCommand` it returns). Substitute your own DEVSWARM_BUILDER_ID for <...>."}
devswarm_prompt.child_reminder	{"v":"💡 anti-hall · devswarm-child-workspace: (per turn) keep the parent orchestrator updated — run `{cli} heartbeat <DEVSWARM_BUILDER_ID> --summary \"<status>\"` to report progress/blockers as you make them — this is what satisfies your Stop-gate report (`send --to-primary --message-file <path>` is a SEPARATE direct message, not a substitute) — and check for + act on any parent messages before continuing, so you stay visible on the parent's task list instead of drifting off it."}
