devswarm_role.pg_escalation	{"v":"Escalation: this neglect signature ({shown}) has been forced-acknowledged {times} times with no observed resolution{intent} — a human should look. This will not repeat automatically after this message. {archive}Next step: run `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox peek-primary <id>` for each flagged id; if it shows unreadCount 0, the gate's count disagrees with the inbox: report it (`~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine defect`) with both numbers instead of acknowledging again. Escape hatch: the user may direct a skip via ~/.anti-hall/skip.json (\"devswarm-parent-gate\")."}
devswarm_role.pg_escalation_archive	{"v":"Every flagged child is done (all required gates set): archive them (`~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh archive <id>`) instead of acknowledging again. "}
devswarm_role.pg_escalation_idle	{"v":"A flagged child is idle with unfinished work (not done, merged and tested): do NOT archive it, that drops its uncommitted or unpushed code. Wake or message it (`~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh send --to <id> ...`) and ask for its status. "}
devswarm_role.pg_escalation_intent	{"v":" (a stated intent was on file for this exact condition, but the absolute backstop was still reached)"}
devswarm_role.pg_flag_app_archived	{"v":"app-archived"}
devswarm_role.pg_flag_archived	{"v":"archived"}
devswarm_role.pg_flag_gone	{"v":"worktree-gone"}
devswarm_role.pg_foreign	{"v":"NOTE — {ids} {verb} registered under a DIFFERENT project (their worktree no longer resolves), so `inbox peek-primary` will refuse them with project-context-mismatch. Read that backlog with `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox read <id>` instead — it is read-only, works from any project, and shows the durable-inbox messages counted above. "}
devswarm_role.pg_frame_head	{"v":"⛔ {guard}: {headline}"}
devswarm_role.pg_frame_indent	{"v":"  "}
devswarm_role.pg_frame_instead	{"v":"Do instead: "}
devswarm_role.pg_frame_override	{"v":"Override (only if the user explicitly asked): "}
devswarm_role.pg_frame_why	{"v":"Why: "}
devswarm_role.pg_gone	{"v":"NOTE — {ids} {verb} a GONE worktree at its recorded path — this cannot be cleared by cd-ing in. WARNING: a MOVED (not retired) worktree reads exactly the same way — this is a path-existence check only, not proof the workspace is dead — and `--ack-as-owner` bypasses ownership with no liveness check of its own, so do not apply it on this signal alone. FIRST inspect with `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox read <id>` (read-only, works from any project/cwd, and will NOT clear this block either way) to see what is actually pending. Only once you have CONFIRMED the workspace is genuinely retired (not just relocated), clear it with `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox ack <id> --ack-as-owner` — the sanctioned cross-workspace-ack override for a confirmed-dead workspace's backlog. "}
devswarm_role.pg_guard_block_window_ms	{"n":0,"v":1800000}
devswarm_role.pg_guard_held	{"v":"Held by anti-hall, not neglected: {ids} last hit the coordinator-work-guard block (it clears by itself); this pass is not counted toward the forced-acknowledgement limit. Message the child to continue. "}
devswarm_role.pg_headline	{"v":"workspace duties need attention before stopping."}
devswarm_role.pg_hour_per_day	{"v":24}
devswarm_role.pg_id_key_prefix	{"v":"id:"}
devswarm_role.pg_ident_unsure_id	{"v":"primary-unresolved"}
devswarm_role.pg_ignore_file	{"v":"ignore.json"}
devswarm_role.pg_inbox_unreadable	{"v":"inbox unreadable"}
devswarm_role.pg_inspect	{"v":"INSPECT the unread backlog via `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox peek-primary <id>` (read-only — does not advance any cursor) to see what is pending for each workspace, then follow up with that workspace as needed; a workspace's own cursor is only advanced by that workspace reading its own inbox, never by this Primary. "}
