devswarm_role.pg_no_session	{"v":"nosession"}
devswarm_role.pg_own_stale	{"v":"YOUR OWN inbound status could not be confirmed: the cached summary predates this reader's live read position (own cursor caught up to or past what the summary last recorded), and a live recheck did not resolve it — treat this as UNKNOWN, not \"no messages\". Check explicitly via `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox count {id}` or `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox read-primary {id}` (then its `ackCommand`) before assuming there is nothing pending. "}
devswarm_role.pg_own_unknown	{"v":"YOUR OWN inbound status could not be confirmed (own-summary unreadable or corrupt — possibly a daemon problem) — treat this as UNKNOWN, not \"no messages\". Check explicitly via `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox read-primary {id}` (then its `ackCommand`; and `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh healthcheck` / `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh logs` to check the daemon) before assuming there is nothing pending. "}
devswarm_role.pg_own_unread	{"v":"YOU (the Primary) have {n} unread parent/peer message(s) — STOP and read them FIRST via `~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine mesh inbox read-primary {id}` (read-only; after handling, run the `ackCommand` it returns). If `mesh inbox peek-primary {id}` shows unreadCount 0, the counts disagree: report it (`~/.anti-hall/ah-engine/bin/ah-engine defect`) rather than re-reading. "}
devswarm_role.pg_parked_joiner	{"v":"\n\n"}
devswarm_role.pg_parked_kid_sep	{"v":", "}
devswarm_role.pg_parked_segment	{"v":"⚠️ anti-hall · devswarm-escalations: not delivered ({n}): the supervisor escalated {kids} (idle — reassign or archive), but this Primary ({id}) is not registered in the mesh store (or its lock was busy), so the notice is PARKED. Run `{cli} register-primary` — the next supervisor sweep then delivers it."}
devswarm_role.pg_plural_s	{"v":"s"}
devswarm_role.pg_poke_prefix	{"v":"[Primary poke]"}
devswarm_role.pg_q_escalation	{"v":"Escalation: {what} has forced-blocked this Stop {times} times with no reply sent — a human should look. This will not repeat automatically after this message (the question itself is still tracked and unresolved). Escape hatch: the user may direct a skip via ~/.anti-hall/skip.json (\"devswarm-parent-gate\")."}
